    <a class="skip-link" href="#maincontent">Skip to main content</a>

    <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Cat care guide</div>
          <h1 id="page-title">Cats FAQ</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="intro">
          Quick answers to the most common questions about cats — from why they purr to how to keep them happy,
          healthy, and delightfully curious.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="faq-shell" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <h2 id="faq-heading" class="sr-only">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="example">
            <summary>Why do cats purr?</summary>
            <div class="details">
              <p>
                Cats purr for more than one reason. They often purr when they feel safe and relaxed, but they may also
                purr to soothe themselves when they are stressed or unwell.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="example">
            <summary>How much sleep do cats need?</summary>
            <div class="details">
              <p>
                Most cats sleep <strong>12 to 16 hours a day</strong>, and kittens or senior cats may sleep even more.
                Their bursts of energy are usually short, intense, and followed by a nap.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="example">
            <summary>What should I feed my cat?</summary>
            <div class="details">
              <p>
                A balanced, complete cat food that matches your cat’s age and health needs is the best starting point.
                Fresh water should always be available, and treats should stay in moderation.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="example">
            <summary>Why do cats knead with their paws?</summary>
            <div class="details">
              <p>
                Kneading is a comforting behavior many cats keep from kittenhood. It can signal contentment, trust,
                and a strong attachment to a cozy spot or favorite person.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="example">
            <summary>How do I make my cat feel at home?</summary>
            <div class="details">
              <p>
                Give your cat quiet places to rest, predictable routines, scratching surfaces, and daily playtime.
                A little patience goes a long way when they are settling into a new space.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>Designed as a simple, accessible FAQ disclosure layout.</footer>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll('.example').forEach((item) => {
        const summary = item.querySelector('summary');

        summary.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          if (event.key === 'Escape' && item.open) {
            item.open = false;
            summary.focus();
          }
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
